The transit example uses figures from Table 3 of the NYC Comptroller’s
Life in the Slow Lane report. The simulated data refresh is illustrative.
https://comptroller.nyc.gov/reports/life-in-the-slow-lane/

The food insecurity example uses the four regional estimates in Table 2 of
Household Food Security in the United States in 2024 (ERR-358), published
by the USDA Economic Research Service. The alternate chart is hypothetical.
https://ers.usda.gov/sites/default/files/_laserfiche/publications/113623/ERR-358.pdf?v=71497

The unemployment example uses first-published and revised seasonally
adjusted 2024 U.S. unemployment rates from the Bureau of Labor Statistics,
Table A and the December estimate in the same release, January 10, 2025.
https://www.bls.gov/news.release/archives/empsit_01102025.htm
